# NON-SECRET names of the three schema-initialization database accounts of the compose example only.
#
# These are the accounts that own the three databases and may therefore create, alter and drop tables.
# They are given to the "db" service, which creates them, and to the one-shot "ofbiz-schema-init"
# service, which authenticates as them - and to NOTHING else. The "ofbiz" service that serves traffic
# is deliberately NOT given this file: it authenticates as the accounts in ofbiz-postgres.env, which
# may read and write rows and may not change the schema.
#
# That is why these three variables live in a file of their own rather than in ofbiz-postgres.env. The
# entry point requires all six OFBIZ_POSTGRES_*_INIT_* variables together or none of them, so a
# serving container that was handed these three names without their passwords is refused - which is
# the intended outcome, but it means the split is load bearing rather than cosmetic.
#
# As with every other tracked file of this example, no password is declared here. The three
# initialization passwords are required Docker Compose variables in docker-compose.yml. See
# "Credentials of the compose example" in DOCKER.adoc.

OFBIZ_POSTGRES_OFBIZ_INIT_USER=ofbizinit

OFBIZ_POSTGRES_OLAP_INIT_USER=ofbizolapinit

OFBIZ_POSTGRES_TENANT_INIT_USER=ofbiztenantinit
